{"key":"F08","report_id":"R0009","kind":"FIELD","label":"uav_architecture_role_and_topology/uav_assisted_mec","status":"OBSERVED","finding":"The system models a multi-UAV assisted MEC network in which K UAVs equipped with edge computing servers circle at a constant altitude to provide communication and computation offloading services to M ground users within their coverage area.","page":3,"locator":"Section III. SYSTEM MODEL AND PROBLEM FORMULATION, paragraph 1","excerpt":"Consider a multi-UAV assisted MEC system, where the network has K UAVs, each of which is equipped with the edge computing server and provides communication and computation services for M GUs.","quantitative":null,"reason":""}
{"key":"F09","report_id":"R0009","kind":"FIELD","label":"partition_and_assignment/gu_uav_split","status":"OBSERVED","finding":"Each ground user's DNN task is split at an optimal partition point so that the first part executes locally on the ground user and the second part is offloaded to a matched UAV within coverage, including full offloading or full local execution as boundary cases.","page":3,"locator":"Section III. SYSTEM MODEL AND PROBLEM FORMULATION, paragraph 3","excerpt":"The first half of each task of the ith GU is executed locally, while the second half of each task of the ith GU is offloaded to the UAV for execution.","quantitative":null,"reason":""}
{"key":"F10","report_id":"R0009","kind":"FIELD","label":"compute_and_radio/compute_and_radio_params","status":"OBSERVED","finding":"The partition analysis configures a 10 MHz wireless channel bandwidth with computing frequencies of 1 GHz for ground user devices and 15 GHz for UAV edge servers.","page":5,"locator":"Section IV.A Optimal Partition Point Selection Algorithm for DNN Tasks, paragraph 2","excerpt":"When the bandwidth condition is 10 MHz, and the computing frequencies of user devices and UAVs are 1 GHz and 15 GHz, respectively","quantitative":null,"reason":""}
