{"key":"F12","report_id":"R0009","kind":"FIELD","label":"sensitivity_and_variability/radius_users_bandwidth","status":"OBSERVED","finding":"Performance evaluations on page 9 examine total system energy consumption and average per-user task processing delay across varying UAV signal coverage radius (Fig. 5), number of ground users (Fig. 6), and communication bandwidth (Fig. 7), showing overhead rises with more ground users and declines with larger coverage radius and bandwidth while DPDTS consistently achieves the lowest energy and delay.","page":9,"locator":"Section V.B Performance Evaluation, paragraphs 2 and 3","excerpt":"Fig. 7 shows the total system energy consumption and each user's average task processing delay obtained by DPDTS and other schemes under different communication bandwidths.","quantitative":null,"reason":""}
{"key":"F13","report_id":"R0009","kind":"NUMBER","label":"total_energy_70_gus","status":"OBSERVED","finding":"When the number of ground users is 70, DPDTS generates a total system energy consumption of 2209.0 J, which is 21.3%, 26.7%, 17.8%, and 48.9% lower than DTS, RAT, EE-PPO, and DPRT, respectively.","page":9,"locator":"Section V.B Performance Evaluation, paragraph 2 (Fig. 6a analysis)","excerpt":"Especially when the number of GUs is 70, the energy consumption generated by DPDTS is 2209.0J, which is 21.3%, 26.7%, 17.8%, and 48.9% lower than that of DTS, RAT, EE-PPO, and DPRT, respectively.","quantitative":{"value":"2209.0","units":"J","baseline":"21.3%, 26.7%, 17.8%, and 48.9% lower than DTS, RAT, EE-PPO, and DPRT, respectively","denominator":"Total system energy consumption across 4 UAVs and 70 ground users per service round averaged over 50 episodes","workload":"ResNet-34, VGG-16, and AlexNet DNN inference tasks with Poisson arrival rate in [0, 5]","conditions":"70 GUs in a 400m x 400m area, 4 UAVs at 50m altitude and 50m coverage radius, 10 MHz bandwidth, 1 GHz GU and 15 GHz UAV computing frequencies"},"reason":""}
{"key":"F14","report_id":"R0010","kind":"FIELD","label":"inference_model_task_and_dataset/cnn_models","status":"OBSERVED","finding":"The system evaluates collaborative pipeline DNN inference across three CNN models (AlexNet, GoogleNet, and VGG-16) using existing UAV trajectory data to model dynamic inter-UAV transmission rates.","page":5,"locator":"Section V.A Simulation Settings, paragraph 2","excerpt":"AlexNet, GoogleNet, and VGG-16. We explore the impact of dynamic data rates between UAVs on the performance of collaborative inference.","quantitative":null,"reason":""}
{"key":"F15","report_id":"R0010","kind":"FIELD","label":"decision_variables_objectives_constraints_and_solver/dqn_action_disassembly","status":"OBSERVED","finding":"To reduce the combinatorial DQN action space for layer allocation across tasks and UAVs, a hierarchical action decomposition pairs one UAV performing a layer-increase action with another UAV performing a corresponding layer-decrease action at each step.","page":4,"locator":"Section IV.B Actions Adaptation, paragraph 2","excerpt":"The increase and decrease actions are paired accordingly, with one UAV performing the increase action while the other UAV generates the corresponding decrease action.","quantitative":null,"reason":""}
{"key":"F16","report_id":"R0010","kind":"FIELD","label":"outcomes_latency_energy_communication_accuracy_reliability_and_scalability/latency_reduction","status":"OBSERVED","finding":"Across both high and low device computational power scenarios and increasing task quantities, the proposed DRL pipeline method consistently achieves the lowest total inference completion latency and smallest latency growth across AlexNet, GoogleNet, and VGG-16 compared to all five benchmark methods.","page":5,"locator":"Section V.B Results Analysis, paragraph 2","excerpt":"We can observe that although the total inference latency of each method increases as the number of tasks increases, our method always performs best under three different models, and the total latency increasing with the growth in inference tasks is the smallest.","quantitative":null,"reason":""}
